WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.720
Two words. Now swap them round:

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.890
«un grand homme», «un homme grand».

3
00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.810
One is a tall man.

4
00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.860
The other is a great man.

5
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:10.130
Which is which?

6
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.030
Now «brave». Put it on
one side of «homme»,

7
00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.680
and he's brave.

8
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:16.830
Put it on the other,

9
00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.680
and he's simply decent.

10
00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.070
Why does one move change the meaning?

11
00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:23.590
And how do you tell which side is which?

12
00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.900
In this mission, you'll sort adjectives
into two zones around a noun,

13
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.360
and find which ones are locked in place.

14
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.810
Then you'll drag «brave», «ancien»
and «propre» before or after

15
00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:37.910
the noun to match the English.

16
00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.250
Your mission: crack the
code of adjective position.
